{{!-- The reply box (the Replying extra), opened under the message it answers (partials/bubble.hbs): posts your reply on X to `replyId`
      (POST /posts/:id/reply). public/js/post-actions.js sends it in place (your bubble joins the chat, the header's
      balance takes the cost). The box shows no price (clean enough to screenshot; the price is in the
      module picker's You send row); while you type, the meta line shows the length, and warns with the price only when
      the text has a link (X's "with URL" row, 13× a plain reply). Without script it posts with a toast back.
      `pictures` (the Pictures add-on, routes/pages.js PICTURE_RULES): photos or a GIF can go with it, added by
      public/js/attach.js (📎, drag and drop, paste; script only: without it the box is text, as before).
      ON A PHONE IT'S X's REPLY SCREEN (the inline composer was cramped on a phone and zoomed in; a
      screen of its own, the message above, Reply at the top right, no zoom): its <dialog> (bubble.hbs) opens full
      screen (`.sheet`, post-actions.js), `.reply-top` shows Cancel and Reply, and the script puts the message you're answering above the box (its face, name, words, "Replying to")
      and your face beside it, joined by THE thread line. The text is 16px on a phone, so iOS doesn't zoom into it.
      Hash: replyId, name (whom you're answering), to (people.replyingView: whom X tags in the reply, "Replying to @a @b
      and 10 others", the full list in THE tooltip; the phone's sheet shows a copy of it under the message,
      post-actions.js sheetContext),
      linkPrice (this account's, routes/pages.js replyBox), pictures, draftText (a draft the account's agent left on the message,
      partials/draft-line.hbs: the box opens holding it). --}}
<form class="reply-form" method="post" action="/posts/{{replyId}}/reply" data-reply data-reply-name="{{name}}" data-link-price="{{rate linkPrice}}"{{#if pictures}} data-pictures="{{pictures}}"{{/if}}>
  <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="{{@root.csrfToken}}">
  <input type="hidden" name="back" value="{{@root.currentPath}}">
  <div class="reply-top"><button type="button" class="btn ghost reply-cancel" data-reply-cancel>Cancel</button><button type="submit" class="pill">Reply</button></div>
  {{#if to}}<p class="replying-to" data-reply-to-line>Replying to {{#each to.shown}}<b>{{this}}</b>{{#unless @last}} {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#if to.more}} and <b class="tip-wide" data-tip="{{to.all}}">{{to.more}} others</b>{{/if}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{!-- THE @HANDLES IN ACCENT, as X's composer: a copy of the text drawn exactly under the box with each @handle
        coloured (post-actions.js `mirror`), the box's own text made transparent once that copy is drawn (.compose.on);
        the caret, the selection and typing stay the box's. Without script, the plain box. --}}
  <div class="compose"><div class="compose-mirror" data-compose-mirror aria-hidden="true"></div><textarea name="text" rows="1" maxlength="4000" placeholder="Reply to {{name}}" aria-label="Reply to {{name}}" required>{{draftText}}</textarea></div>
  <div class="reply-foot">
    <span class="reply-meta" data-reply-meta></span>
    <button type="submit" class="pill">Reply</button>
  </div>
</form>
